    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1231">

                <pb facs="0863" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/327.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent Canova.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 4. Consul, Tampico, reports that local authorities have not yet
                    received orders to accept New York exchange at prevailing rate. Confer with
                    Hanna and request that such order be repeated at once and that it also be sent
                    Tuxpam authorities since Consul states that production taxes in Panuco Topila
                    fields must be paid in Tuxpam July 15.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
